    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0863" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.5/5–1754: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-17T22:00:00+01:00">May 17, 1954—10 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dulte 79. Repeated information Paris 286, London 176. Paris eyes only Ambassador.
                    London eyes only Ambassador. Re Dulte 77, repeated Paris 283.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d543-f1"/> Caccia has just informed us that Eden has gotten off
                    telegram to London recommending approval of immediate start of five-power
                    military staff talks. He has asked for reply by tomorrow and believes it will be
                    favorable. His only reservation will be that <pb facs="0864" n="838"
                        xml:id="pg838"/> committee which is to start its work in Washington should
                    have power to move to meeting place other than Washington if later developments
                    would indicate such move desirable.</p>
                <p>Re Dulte 76, (repeated Paris 282, London 173) Caccia reported subject had gone
                    well in Parliament this afternoon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d543-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
